 "names_note": "PROVISIONAL names, manufactured and meant to be replaced by ear. Each is <bank>_sample_<size>_<loop>: the bank from which of the two tone banks references this wave -- 0x080fba78 for music, 0x080fc138 for effects -- the size band from the record length, and looping or oneshot from whether the record carries a loop point. `unbanked` means neither bank points at it directly, because a tone entry of type 0x40 or 0x80 reaches a keysplit or percussion sub-table instead, and those were not followed. Ties take a Greek-letter suffix. `name` keeps the ROM-ordered wave_<nn> identity; only `source` and `provisional_name` carry the manufactured one. Nothing here names an instrument: the banks are custom, not General MIDI, so a program number does not imply what it sounds like."
